e() taxonomy in AC2 covers only timed-out / cancelled / failed. A superseded run (a newer patchset triggering concurrency cancel-in-progress) surfaces its jobs as plain 'cancelled', so the enriched message will not distinguish superseded from an operator/system cancel — one of the exact ambiguities the plan set out to remove.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f417128b52d2b8a28","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 1 / AC2","norm_id":"n65a2f2ec98390134","priority":0.2063,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["A newer patchset supersedes an in-flight run; the operator sees 'cancelled' jobs but cannot tell it was a supersede vs a manual/system cancel","The whole run (including the vote job) is itself cancelled by cancel-in-progress, so neither the cast nor the enriched comment posts at all"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] De-risk the 'no --label = comment, not vote' assumption with a one-off probe against the real Gerrit (or cite prior evidence) and record that the message-only SSH call leaves Verified/Code-Review untouched.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T6","T7","T9"],"criteria":["T2","E6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Approach: 'passing NO --label so it is a comment and not a vote'","AC4 asserts a test 'parsing gerrit-verify.yaml for that step and failing if --label, Verified= or Code-Review= appears in it' — this proves the command text, not Gerrit's runtime behavior","This is a newer integration point (a hand-rolled SSH call rather than the vetted action) whose no-label-means-no-vote behavior is genuinely load-bearing given the OBSERVABILITY-ONLY constraint"],"finding":"The core claim that a `gerrit review --message` call with NO `--label` posts a comment WITHOUT casting a vote is an assertion about Gerrit's behavior that no in-session or live check exercises; AC4 only greps the workflow YAML for the absence of `--label`.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fff35efa6f415d917","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 2; AC4","norm_id":"nd797f99c91700d7e","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["If a bare `--message` SSH call unexpectedly resets or re-casts a label on some Gerrit versions, the observability-only guarantee is violated in production despite all offline tests passing"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add a spike note or evidence line confirming a `gerrit review <c>,<p> --message '...'` with no --label leaves labels unchanged on the target Gerrit version, mirroring the 'Verified both at the pinned SHA' diligence already shown for the action.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily